    62	## Remaining first-render cost
    63	
    64	Three production profiles of the final candidate put the median active browser time at 37.63 ms under the profiler. The median self time is 6.33 ms in core orchestration, 5.49 ms in native main-thread work, 3.36 ms in layout and formatting, 2.58 ms in DOM code (including 1.66 ms in the interaction module), 2.01 ms in theme resolution, 1.64 ms in scales and view, 1.22 ms in normalization, 1.20 ms in drawing, 1.02 ms in reader work and 0.76 ms in scene construction. Another 10.02 ms is unattributed JavaScript, including harness work. The browser's accessibility tree has no isolated time in these samples. The on-demand tooltip and table rendering have no distinct sampled cost. The active compact profile attributes 11.47 ms to theme work across 40 charts. [Final P1 profile](profiles/2026-11-22/final/20261122T052750Z-first-trend-axylo.summary.json) · [Final P8 profile](profiles/2026-11-22/final/20261122T052755Z-compact-trend-axylo.summary.json)
    65	
    66	The remaining work to reach 10 ms would include eliminating forced style and layout reads across chart creation, reducing first-use locale formatting, and deferring interaction setup that can safely wait for first focus or input. Those changes need separate prototypes and profiles. The generated description, synchronous diagnostics and first-frame drawing are required behaviors. The sampled costs do not establish that those changes alone could save 17.40 ms.
    67	
    68	Proposal for the owner: set the 1.0 P1 budget to 30 ms for the same workload and reference desktop. The candidate recorded 27.40 ms in 20 runs, giving 2.60 ms of margin. The owner-accepted baseline was 29.42 ms. Keep 10 ms as a target for the recurring improvement work. The product specification still requires 10 ms.
